211 0 obj
<</E(The first layer contains the places where data originates. The base map is assembled from satellite and aerial imagery, from street-level images captured by camera-equipped vehicles, and from authoritative datasets supplied by governments and mapping agencies, such as road networks, boundaries, and address records. Business and place details come from owner-submitted listings and from user contributions including reviews, photographs, and corrections, while public transport timetables arrive as structured feeds from transit agencies.)/K[ 13]/P 84 0 R /Pg 14 0 R /S/H3/T(The first layer contains the places where data originates. The base map is assembled from satellite and aerial imagery, from street-level images captured by camera-equipped vehicles, and from authoritative datasets supplied by governments and mapping agencies, such as road networks, boundaries, and address records. Business and place details come from owner-submitted listings and from user contributions including reviews, photographs, and corrections, while public transport timetables arrive as structured feeds from transit agencies.)/Type/StructElem>>
endobj
212 0 obj
<</E(The most dynamic source is the stream of location signals from the phones of travellers who have chosen to share them. Each signal holds a position, a timestamp, and a speed estimate, and when millions of such records are aggregated and anonymised they reveal how fast traffic is moving on every road segment at that moment. Together these sources show the variety dimension of big data: images, geometries, tables, text, and telemetry at once.)/K[ 14]/P 84 0 R /Pg 14 0 R /S/H3/T(The most dynamic source is the stream of location signals from the phones of travellers who have chosen to share them. Each signal holds a position, a timestamp, and a speed estimate, and when millions of such records are aggregated and anonymised they reveal how fast traffic is moving on every road segment at that moment. Together these sources show the variety dimension of big data: images, geometries, tables, text, and telemetry at once.)/Type/StructElem>>
endobj
213 0 obj
<</E(Big data refers to information thatis too large, too fast, or too varied to be captured, stored, and analysed with traditional single-machine databases. It is usually described through the five Vs: volume, the quantity of records; velocity, the speed of arrival; variety, the mixture of tables, logs, images, and text; veracity, the trustworthiness of noisy data; and value, the insight that justifies the cost. Mapping a big data process means tracing data from the moment it is generated to the moment it influences a decision shown to a user.)/K[ 15]/P 84 0 R /Pg 14 0 R /S/H3/T(Big data refers to information thatis too large, too fast, or too varied to be captured, stored, and analysed with traditional single-machine databases. It is usually described through the five Vs: volume, the quantity of records; velocity, the speed of arrival; variety, the mixture of tables, logs, images, and text; veracity, the trustworthiness of noisy data; and value, the insight that justifies the cost. Mapping a big data process means tracing data from the moment it is generated to the moment it influences a decision shown to a user.)/Type/StructElem>>
endobj
214 0 obj
<</E(The group selected Google Maps as its case study and organised the data flow under four headings: data sources, storage, processing, and output. It combines slowly changing planet-scale map data with live traffic data that changes every few seconds. The map presented here is a simplified, educational model built from publicly available descriptions; the internal architecture of a commercial product is proprietary, so the stages should be read as a representative pipeline rather than an official blueprint.)/K[ 16]/P 84 0 R /Pg 14 0 R /S/H3/T(The group selected Google Maps as its case study and organised the data flow under four headings: data sources, storage, processing, and output. It combines slowly changing planet-scale map data with live traffic data that changes every few seconds. The map presented here is a simplified, educational model built from publicly available descriptions; the internal architecture of a commercial product is proprietary, so the stages should be read as a representative pipeline rather than an official blueprint.)/Type/StructElem>>
endobj
