259 0 obj
<</E(Machine learning builds programs that improveat a task by learning patterns from data instead of following hand-written rules. A project is therefore a disciplined sequence of stages, each producing an output that feeds the next and each able to send the team back to an earlier stage when results disappoint. The group's task was to draw this sequence as a flowchart covering data collection, feature extraction, algorithm selection, training, testing, and evaluation, and to explain every symbol in it.)/K[ 25]/P 86 0 R /Pg 16 0 R /S/H4/T(Machine learning builds programs that improveat a task by learning patterns from data instead of following hand-written rules. A project is therefore a disciplined sequence of stages, each producing an output that feeds the next and each able to send the team back to an earlier stage when results disappoint. The group's task was to draw this sequence as a flowchart covering data collection, feature extraction, algorithm selection, training, testing, and evaluation, and to explain every symbol in it.)/Type/StructElem>>
endobj
260 0 obj
<</E(To keep the chart concrete, a familiar supervised problem was used as a running example: predicting whether a telecom subscriber will cancel the service next month, known as customer churn prediction. The target is a yes-or-no label, so this is binary classification. The flowchart starts with a terminator symbol and a process box that defines the problem and success criteria, and then uses rectangles for processing steps, parallelograms for data input and output, diamonds for decisions, and arrows for the direction of flow.)/K[ 26]/P 86 0 R /Pg 16 0 R /S/H4/T(To keep the chart concrete, a familiar supervised problem was used as a running example: predicting whether a telecom subscriber will cancel the service next month, known as customer churn prediction. The target is a yes-or-no label, so this is binary classification. The flowchart starts with a terminator symbol and a process box that defines the problem and success criteria, and then uses rectangles for processing steps, parallelograms for data input and output, diamonds for decisions, and arrows for the direction of flow.)/Type/StructElem>>
endobj
261 0 obj
<</E(The first working stage is data collection. For the churn example the team gathers billing records, call and data-usage logs, support tickets, and contract details, and joins them on a customer identifier so that each row describes one subscriber and carries a label showing whether that subscriber left. At this point the team asks whether the data is large enough, representative of future customers, and legally permitted for this use.)/K[ 27]/P 86 0 R /Pg 16 0 R /S/H4/T(The first working stage is data collection. For the churn example the team gathers billing records, call and data-usage logs, support tickets, and contract details, and joins them on a customer identifier so that each row describes one subscriber and carries a label showing whether that subscriber left. At this point the team asks whether the data is large enough, representative of future customers, and legally permitted for this use.)/Type/StructElem>>
endobj
262 0 obj
<</E(Raw data is rarely ready for learning, so the next box is cleaning and preprocessing. Missing values are removed or filled with the median, the most frequent category, or a predicted value; duplicates are dropped; impossible entries such as negative call durations are corrected; and outliers are examined rather than deleted blindly. Categorical fields such as contract type are converted to numbers by one-hot encoding, and numeric fields are standardised so that columns with large units do not dominate.)/K[ 28]/P 86 0 R /Pg 16 0 R /S/H4/T(Raw data is rarely ready for learning, so the next box is cleaning and preprocessing. Missing values are removed or filled with the median, the most frequent category, or a predicted value; duplicates are dropped; impossible entries such as negative call durations are corrected; and outliers are examined rather than deleted blindly. Categorical fields such as contract type are converted to numbers by one-hot encoding, and numeric fields are standardised so that columns with large units do not dominate.)/Type/StructElem>>
endobj
