1234 0 obj
<</Dest[ 14 0 R /Fit]/Next 1248 0 R /Parent 1223 0 R /Title(Big data refers to information thatis too large, too fast, or too varied to be captured, stored, and analysed with traditional single-machine databases. It is usually described through the five Vs: volume, the quantity of records; velocity, the speed of arrival; variety, the mixture of tables, logs, images, and text; veracity, the trustworthiness of noisy data; and value, the insight that justifies the cost. Mapping a big data process means tracing data from the moment it is generated to the moment it influences a decision shown to a user.)>>
endobj
