1284 0 obj
<</Dest[ 16 0 R /Fit]/Next 1285 0 R /Parent 1278 0 R /Title(Machine learning builds programs that improveat a task by learning patterns from data instead of following hand-written rules. A project is therefore a disciplined sequence of stages, each producing an output that feeds the next and each able to send the team back to an earlier stage when results disappoint. The group's task was to draw this sequence as a flowchart covering data collection, feature extraction, algorithm selection, training, testing, and evaluation, and to explain every symbol in it.)>>
endobj
1285 0 obj
<</Dest[ 16 0 R /Fit]/Parent 1278 0 R /Prev 1284 0 R /Title(To keep the chart concrete, a familiar supervised problem was used as a running example: predicting whether a telecom subscriber will cancel the service next month, known as customer churn prediction. The target is a yes-or-no label, so this is binary classification. The flowchart starts with a terminator symbol and a process box that defines the problem and success criteria, and then uses rectangles for processing steps, parallelograms for data input and output, diamonds for decisions, and arrows for the direction of flow.)>>
endobj
