1316 0 obj
<</Dest[ 19 0 R /Fit]/Next 1317 0 R /Parent 1312 0 R /Title(Backpropagation isthe algorithm that makes the training of neural networks practical. A network is a chain of simple mathematical operations, and training means adjusting its weights so that its output moves closer to the desired answer. Backpropagation first runs an input forward through the network to obtain a prediction, then measures the error, and finally applies the chain rule of calculus backwards from the output to every weight, revealing how much each weight contributed to the error and in which direction it should move. The group used a deliberately small network so that every number could be checked by hand.)>>
endobj
